KG42.register("nodes-372f0e9bc147c0df928e9d95",{"id":"KG40-a82c49d45641943a","code":"CLR060.2","label":"Balanced trade allocation subject to price-based trading permission","definition":"Allocate purchase and sale quantities in the same auction round so that the total accepted supply and demand balance and the allocation eligibility conditions for buy and sell bids relative to the clearing price are satisfied.","layer":"L5","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"clearing.local","concept_ids":["clearing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: accepted purchase and sale quantities in the same auction round","Allocation conditions: accepted-quantity balance and two-sided price eligibility","Statement type: quantity allocation and feasible bounds"]},"exclusions":[["Consumption and production bids enter the same clearing round, and within the accepted bid range, Σ_{i=1}^{n_B}d_i=Σ_{j=1}^{n_S}s_j is maintained.","A buy price p_i^{bid}≥p^M permits a purchase allocation, and a sell price p_j^{offer}≤p^M permits a sale allocation; eligibility does not mean full-volume execution.","In the original expression, d_i and s_j are called bid quantities, and the accepted-quantity range is restricted by the accompanying text; no same-price rationing rules are given.","Clearing occurs every 15 min, using a 24 h rolling trading look-ahead; unmet demand may continue to be submitted in subsequent periods."]],"members":[{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"If a local clearing round leaves energy demand unfulfilled, the prosumer may continue submitting demand bids in subsequent trading cycles. Scope: Demand-side rebidding across successive trading cycles in the modeled LEM. Condition: A local clearing round does not fulfill the prosumer's energy demand. After each local clearing round, remaining unaccepted demand bids have their prices gradually increased until buying prosumers offer their highest willingness to pay in the final time step before delivery. Scope: Buying-side bid-price updates before delivery in the modeled LEM. Condition: Demand bids remain wholly or partly unaccepted after a local clearing round. Demand bids are submitted at intervals in a standardized bid format. Scope: Demand submissions in the modeled centralized two-sided auction. Prosumers must decide the quantity and pricing of their demand bids before the delivery interval. Scope: Pre-delivery demand bidding in the modeled LEM. Bid quantities are based on electrical demand or generation forecasting calculated using model predictive control. Scope: Quantity determination for demand bids under the modeled bidding strategy. Demand-bid prices use a linear trading strategy, with buying prosumers aiming to purchase energy at the lowest price initially. Scope: Initial buying-side bid pricing in the modeled LEM. The prosumer-selected trading horizon can range from 6 to 24 h. Scope: Demand-side application of the modeled prosumer bidding strategy.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Buying-side bid-price updates before delivery in the modeled LEM. | Demand submissions in the modeled centralized two-sided auction. | Demand-side application of the modeled prosumer bidding strategy. | Demand-side rebidding across successive trading cycles in the modeled LEM. | Initial buying-side bid pricing in the modeled LEM. | Pre-delivery demand bidding in the modeled LEM. | Quantity determination for demand bids under the modeled bidding strategy.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e15"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","source_rule_sha256":"87e7776c709302da81dff05b3f83bb6805fec30ec90eaa778b25085c4f9f7b38","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Demand submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. Supply submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. Demand submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. Supply submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. The local market operator coordinates clearing by ensuring balance between total accepted consumption and generation. Scope: Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. Buyers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a purchase allocation. Scope: Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a sale allocation. Scope: Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The seller's offer price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM clears every 15 min with a 24 h trading horizon. Scope: Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. Local clearing must balance total accepted demand and total accepted supply. Scope: The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. | Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. | Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities. | The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C005","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C006","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C007","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C008","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C009"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1a48a3ca7bf338b63c7eadeda4cf87b884cede3824a558f1a1e72f6dcbf1df91","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Demand bids are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Supply offers are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Local market clearing occurs before the physical energy exchange at the delivery time step. Scope: Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. Buyers may purchase energy when their bid price meets or exceeds the uniform local market price. Scope: Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers may sell energy when their offered price does not exceed the uniform local market price. Scope: Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The seller's offered price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM permits electricity trading up to 24 h in advance of delivery. Scope: Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. | Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation. | Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. | Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C003"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"8625e846a0dbcb8eacf18cc908b4bf6523c5cea0eecea164bf38bfdf4df4269a","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","market_meaning":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. In the reported transition-time case, synchronized demand-bid submissions for the same delivery time cause an increase in local market clearing prices. Scope: Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM. Condition: Multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously and submit bids for the same delivery time. The local auction uses uniform pricing. Scope: Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. | Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction. | Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"8bf8f0ca152c3dc6cfa5233cf8b0b1b2ff52401389fa0044f1cb7ab2545a0592","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["45-heat_pump_flexibility"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Limited by the scope, the description of other parts of lemlab is omitted Th in this work. However, ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The LEM uses a future market design, which is the most common market design found in the literature [29]. Therefore, the LEM undergoes clearing every 15 min, with a 24 h trading horizon, allowing prosumers to trade electricity up to 24 h in advance. This allows the LEM to function as a day-ahead, intraday, or near real-time market. If prosumers are unable to fulfill their energy demand in one round of market clearing, they can continue submitting their bids in subsequent trading cycles. During settlement, any energy imbalances resulting from a deviation from the traded position lead to additional balancing costs.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"The LEM uses a future market design, which is the most common market design found in the literature [29]. Therefore, the LEM undergoes clearing every 15 min, with a 24 h trading horizon, allowing prosumers to trade electricity up to 24 h in advance. This allows the LEM to function as a day-ahead, intraday, or near real-time market. If prosumers are unable to fulfill their energy demand in one round of market clearing, they can continue submitting their bids in subsequent trading cycles. During settlement, any energy imbalances resulting from a deviation from the traded position lead to additional balancing costs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ed The double-sided auction process is visualized in Fig. 3. The uniform le pricing for the double-s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Prosumers must decide on the quantity and pricing of their bids prior to the delivery interval. The bid quantity is based on electrical demand or generation forecasting, calculated using model predictive control discussed in Section 2.3. A linear trading strategy is used for the bid prices. Prosumers who buy energy aim to purchase it at the lowest price initially. After each round of market clearing, any remaining unaccepted bids' prices gradually increase until prosumers offer the highest price they are willing to pay in the final time step before the delivery period. Conversely, prosumers who sell energy begin by bidding at the highest price and gradually decrease the price as the delivery time approaches. This behavior is described by the following equation:","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"Prosumers must decide on the quantity and pricing of their bids prior to the delivery interval. The bid quantity is based on electrical demand or generation forecasting, calculated using model predictive control discussed in Section 2.3. A linear trading strategy is used for the bid prices. Prosumers who buy energy aim to purchase it at the lowest price initially. After each round of market clearing, any remaining unaccepted bids' prices gradually increase until prosumers offer the highest price they are willing to pay in the final time step before the delivery period. Conversely, prosumers who sell energy begin by bidding at the highest price and gradually decrease the price as the delivery time approaches. This behavior is described by the following equation:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ed The double-sided auction process is visualized in Fig. 3. The uniform le pricing for the double-s","equation_id":"2-4","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"p_{t,bid} = p_{max} − (t_d − t)Δp, ∀ t_d − ΔT ⩽ t ⩽ t_d (2)\np_{t,offer} = p_{min} + (t_d − t)Δp, ∀ t_d − ΔT ⩽ t ⩽ t_d (3)\nΔp = (p_{max} − p_{min}) / ΔT (4)\nwhere t and t_d represent the current time step and the delivery period. p_{max} and p_{min} are the price ceiling and floor. ΔT is the trading horizon selected by the prosumer, which can range from 6 to 24 h. Δp is the price increment in the next time step when the bids are not accepted completely.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"p_{t,bid} = p_{max} − (t_d − t)Δp, ∀ t_d − ΔT ⩽ t ⩽ t_d (2)\np_{t,offer} = p_{min} + (t_d − t)Δp, ∀ t_d − ΔT ⩽ t ⩽ t_d (3)\nΔp = (p_{max} − p_{min}) / ΔT (4)\nwhere t and t_d represent the current time step and the delivery period. p_{max} and p_{min} are the price ceiling and floor. ΔT is the trading horizon selected by the prosumer, which can range from 6 to 24 h. Δp is the price increment in the next time step when the bids are not accepted completely."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The two-sided auction allows for consumption and production bids to be part of the same market clearing process. The market operator ensures a balance between total consumption and total generation among the accepted bids.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The two-sided auction allows for consumption and production bids to be part of the same market clearing process. The market operator ensures a balance between total consumption and total generation among the accepted bids."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on to the optimal schedules prior to","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In general, prosumers must complete the following steps to achieve energy exchange in the LEM:\n1. forecasts: make forecasts about weather, demands, and electricity prices;\n2. model-predictive control: use the model-predictive control (MPC) to generate the optimal schedules for their flexible loads such HPs, EVs, and batteries;\n3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on the optimal schedules prior to the delivery time\n4. market clearing: match the demand and supply and clear the market;\n5. receiving results: receives the market clearing results for the delivery time after the market clearing;\n6. real-time control: use real-time controller to adjust the operating states of the flexible loads at the delivery time according to the electricity procured from the LEM;\n7. settlement: settle the consumption or generation soon after the electricity has been delivered\n\nThe steps 1 to 5 should be repeated for every rolling horizon prior to the delivery time step. Prosumers should check the clearing results from the previous rolling horizon to ensure that the procured electricity is sufficient for their energy demand at the time step of delivery.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"In general, prosumers must complete the following steps to achieve energy exchange in the LEM:\n1. forecasts: make forecasts about weather, demands, and electricity prices;\n2. model-predictive control: use the model-predictive control (MPC) to generate the optimal schedules for their flexible loads such HPs, EVs, and batteries;\n3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on the optimal schedules prior to the delivery time\n4. market clearing: match the demand and supply and clear the market;\n5. receiving results: receives the market clearing results for the delivery time after the market clearing;\n6. real-time control: use real-time controller to adjust the operating states of the flexible loads at the delivery time according to the electricity procured from the LEM;\n7. settlement: settle the consumption or generation soon after the electricity has been delivered\n\nThe steps 1 to 5 should be repeated for every rolling horizon prior to the delivery time step. Prosumers should check the clearing results from the previous rolling horizon to ensure that the procured electricity is sufficient for their energy demand at the time step of delivery."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Limited by the scope, the description of other parts of lemlab is omitted Th in this work. However, ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The LEM uses a future market design, which is the most common market design found in the literature [29]. Therefore, the LEM undergoes clearing every 15 min, with a 24 h trading horizon, allowing prosumers to trade electricity up to 24 h in advance. This allows the LEM to function as a day-ahead, intraday, or near real-time market. If prosumers are unable to fulfill their energy demand in one round of market clearing, they can continue submitting their bids in subsequent trading cycles. During settlement, any energy imbalances resulting from a deviation from the traded position lead to additional balancing costs.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The LEM uses a future market design, which is the most common market design found in the literature [29]. Therefore, the LEM undergoes clearing every 15 min, with a 24 h trading horizon, allowing prosumers to trade electricity up to 24 h in advance. This allows the LEM to function as a day-ahead, intraday, or near real-time market. If prosumers are unable to fulfill their energy demand in one round of market clearing, they can continue submitting their bids in subsequent trading cycles. During settlement, any energy imbalances resulting from a deviation from the traded position lead to additional balancing costs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"max SW = ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} u_i(d_i) − ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} c_j(s_j)\ns.t. ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j (1)","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"max SW = ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} u_i(d_i) − ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} c_j(s_j)\ns.t. ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j (1)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on to the optimal schedules prior to","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In general, prosumers must complete the following steps to achieve energy exchange in the LEM:\n1. forecasts: make forecasts about weather, demands, and electricity prices;\n2. model-predictive control: use the model-predictive control (MPC) to generate the optimal schedules for their flexible loads such HPs, EVs, and batteries;\n3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on the optimal schedules prior to the delivery time\n4. market clearing: match the demand and supply and clear the market;\n5. receiving results: receives the market clearing results for the delivery time after the market clearing;\n6. real-time control: use real-time controller to adjust the operating states of the flexible loads at the delivery time according to the electricity procured from the LEM;\n7. settlement: settle the consumption or generation soon after the electricity has been delivered\n\nThe steps 1 to 5 should be repeated for every rolling horizon prior to the delivery time step. Prosumers should check the clearing results from the previous rolling horizon to ensure that the procured electricity is sufficient for their energy demand at the time step of delivery.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"In general, prosumers must complete the following steps to achieve energy exchange in the LEM:\n1. forecasts: make forecasts about weather, demands, and electricity prices;\n2. model-predictive control: use the model-predictive control (MPC) to generate the optimal schedules for their flexible loads such HPs, EVs, and batteries;\n3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on the optimal schedules prior to the delivery time\n4. market clearing: match the demand and supply and clear the market;\n5. receiving results: receives the market clearing results for the delivery time after the market clearing;\n6. real-time control: use real-time controller to adjust the operating states of the flexible loads at the delivery time according to the electricity procured from the LEM;\n7. settlement: settle the consumption or generation soon after the electricity has been delivered\n\nThe steps 1 to 5 should be repeated for every rolling horizon prior to the delivery time step. Prosumers should check the clearing results from the previous rolling horizon to ensure that the procured electricity is sufficient for their energy demand at the time step of delivery."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. Timeline of the trading process in the LEM. to su Otherwise, they should continue bidding at","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Otherwise, they should continue bidding at later time steps until they have obtained enough electricity. During the delivery time step, the physical flow of energy takes place, and real-time control is activated to ensure precise consumption. Finally, the costs are settled based on the metering data that reflects the real consumption. The whole process is illustrated in Fig. 2.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Otherwise, they should continue bidding at later time steps until they have obtained enough electricity. During the delivery time step, the physical flow of energy takes place, and real-time control is activated to ensure precise consumption. Finally, the costs are settled based on the metering data that reflects the real consumption. The whole process is illustrated in Fig. 2."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a so ute educt o o t e e e gy su p us s a ecause o t e lower solar radiation in winter. cl The compa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"LEMs aim to provide advantageous electricity prices by facilitating lower local market prices for all participants. Energy buyers can save costs by using electricity cheaper than the retailer prices, while energy sellers can earn more money compared to direct sales to the retailer. These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process.","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","quote":"LEMs aim to provide advantageous electricity prices by facilitating lower local market prices for all participants. Energy buyers can save costs by using electricity cheaper than the retailer prices, while energy sellers can earn more money compared to direct sales to the retailer. These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["balanced_auction_allocation"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG40-L5-SC-L5-ce2697ec42590f31","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L5","ontological_kind":"SC-L5-ce2697ec42590f31"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"Allocate purchase and sale quantities in the same auction round so that the total accepted supply and demand balance and the allocation eligibility conditions for buy and sell bids relative to the clearing price are satisfied.","identity_fields":["Object: accepted purchase and sale quantities in the same auction round","Allocation conditions: accepted-quantity balance and two-sided price eligibility","Statement type: quantity allocation and feasible bounds"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","paper_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"clearing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"If a local clearing round leaves energy demand unfulfilled, the prosumer may continue submitting demand bids in subsequent trading cycles. Scope: Demand-side rebidding across successive trading cycles in the modeled LEM. Condition: A local clearing round does not fulfill the prosumer's energy demand. After each local clearing round, remaining unaccepted demand bids have their prices gradually increased until buying prosumers offer their highest willingness to pay in the final time step before delivery. Scope: Buying-side bid-price updates before delivery in the modeled LEM. Condition: Demand bids remain wholly or partly unaccepted after a local clearing round. Demand bids are submitted at intervals in a standardized bid format. Scope: Demand submissions in the modeled centralized two-sided auction. Prosumers must decide the quantity and pricing of their demand bids before the delivery interval. Scope: Pre-delivery demand bidding in the modeled LEM. Bid quantities are based on electrical demand or generation forecasting calculated using model predictive control. Scope: Quantity determination for demand bids under the modeled bidding strategy. Demand-bid prices use a linear trading strategy, with buying prosumers aiming to purchase energy at the lowest price initially. Scope: Initial buying-side bid pricing in the modeled LEM. The prosumer-selected trading horizon can range from 6 to 24 h. Scope: Demand-side application of the modeled prosumer bidding strategy.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Buying-side bid-price updates before delivery in the modeled LEM. | Demand submissions in the modeled centralized two-sided auction. | Demand-side application of the modeled prosumer bidding strategy. | Demand-side rebidding across successive trading cycles in the modeled LEM. | Initial buying-side bid pricing in the modeled LEM. | Pre-delivery demand bidding in the modeled LEM. | Quantity determination for demand bids under the modeled bidding strategy.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e15"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","source_rule_sha256":"87e7776c709302da81dff05b3f83bb6805fec30ec90eaa778b25085c4f9f7b38"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Demand submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. Supply submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. Demand submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. Supply submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery. The local market operator coordinates clearing by ensuring balance between total accepted consumption and generation. Scope: Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. Buyers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a purchase allocation. Scope: Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a sale allocation. Scope: Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The seller's offer price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM clears every 15 min with a 24 h trading horizon. Scope: Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. Local clearing must balance total accepted demand and total accepted supply. Scope: The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction. | Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction. | Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM. | Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. | The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities. | The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C005","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C006","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C007","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C008","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C009"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1a48a3ca7bf338b63c7eadeda4cf87b884cede3824a558f1a1e72f6dcbf1df91"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Demand bids are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Supply offers are submitted before the physical energy exchange at delivery. Scope: Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. Local market clearing occurs before the physical energy exchange at the delivery time step. Scope: Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. Buyers may purchase energy when their bid price meets or exceeds the uniform local market price. Scope: Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price. Sellers may sell energy when their offered price does not exceed the uniform local market price. Scope: Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. Condition: The seller's offered price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price. The LEM permits electricity trading up to 24 h in advance of delivery. Scope: Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Buyer-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Demand submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow. | Future-market trading in the study LEM, including day-ahead, intraday and near real-time operation. | Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM. | Seller-side trading permission in the uniform-price, two-sided LEM auction. | Supply submission in the study's pre-delivery LEM workflow.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C003"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"8625e846a0dbcb8eacf18cc908b4bf6523c5cea0eecea164bf38bfdf4df4269a"},{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","market_meaning":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. In the reported transition-time case, synchronized demand-bid submissions for the same delivery time cause an increase in local market clearing prices. Scope: Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM. Condition: Multiple prosumers plan to run their heat pumps simultaneously and submit bids for the same delivery time. The local auction uses uniform pricing. Scope: Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market. | Pricing design of the proposed centralized two-sided local auction. | Reported transition-time simulation of the residential heat-pump LEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"8bf8f0ca152c3dc6cfa5233cf8b0b1b2ff52401389fa0044f1cb7ab2545a0592"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"If a local clearing round leaves energy demand unfulfilled, the prosumer may continue submitting demand bids in subsequent trading cycles. Scope: Demand-side rebidding across successive trading cycles in the modeled LEM. Condition: A local clearing round does not fulfill the prosumer's energy demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Limited by the scope, the description of other parts of lemlab is omitted Th in this work. However, ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The LEM uses a future market design, which is the most common market design found in the literature [29]. Therefore, the LEM undergoes clearing every 15 min, with a 24 h trading horizon, allowing prosumers to trade electricity up to 24 h in advance. This allows the LEM to function as a day-ahead, intraday, or near real-time market. If prosumers are unable to fulfill their energy demand in one round of market clearing, they can continue submitting their bids in subsequent trading cycles. During settlement, any energy imbalances resulting from a deviation from the traded position lead to additional balancing costs."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"After each local clearing round, remaining unaccepted demand bids have their prices gradually increased until buying prosumers offer their highest willingness to pay in the final time step before delivery. Scope: Buying-side bid-price updates before delivery in the modeled LEM. Condition: Demand bids remain wholly or partly unaccepted after a local clearing round.","expression":"p_{t,bid} = p_{max} - (t_d - t)\\Delta p, \\quad \\forall\\, t_d - \\Delta T \\le t \\le t_d; \\quad \\Delta p = (p_{max} - p_{min}) / \\Delta T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001-X002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-P001","v141-c-R001-P002","v141-c-R001-P003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e15"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ed The double-sided auction process is visualized in Fig. 3. The uniform le pricing for the double-s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Prosumers must decide on the quantity and pricing of their bids prior to the delivery interval. The bid quantity is based on electrical demand or generation forecasting, calculated using model predictive control discussed in Section 2.3. A linear trading strategy is used for the bid prices. Prosumers who buy energy aim to purchase it at the lowest price initially. After each round of market clearing, any remaining unaccepted bids' prices gradually increase until prosumers offer the highest price they are willing to pay in the final time step before the delivery period. Conversely, prosumers who sell energy begin by bidding at the highest price and gradually decrease the price as the delivery time approaches. This behavior is described by the following equation:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ed The double-sided auction process is visualized in Fig. 3. The uniform le pricing for the double-s","equation_id":"2-4","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"p_{t,bid} = p_{max} − (t_d − t)Δp, ∀ t_d − ΔT ⩽ t ⩽ t_d (2)\np_{t,offer} = p_{min} + (t_d − t)Δp, ∀ t_d − ΔT ⩽ t ⩽ t_d (3)\nΔp = (p_{max} − p_{min}) / ΔT (4)\nwhere t and t_d represent the current time step and the delivery period. p_{max} and p_{min} are the price ceiling and floor. ΔT is the trading horizon selected by the prosumer, which can range from 6 to 24 h. Δp is the price increment in the next time step when the bids are not accepted completely."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Demand submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Consumption bids in the modeled local two-sided auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e11"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The two-sided auction allows for consumption and production bids to be part of the same market clearing process. The market operator ensures a balance between total consumption and total generation among the accepted bids."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply submissions are inputs to the local market clearing process. Scope: Production offers in the modeled local two-sided auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e11"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The two-sided auction allows for consumption and production bids to be part of the same market clearing process. The market operator ensures a balance between total consumption and total generation among the accepted bids."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Demand submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on to the optimal schedules prior to","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In general, prosumers must complete the following steps to achieve energy exchange in the LEM:\n1. forecasts: make forecasts about weather, demands, and electricity prices;\n2. model-predictive control: use the model-predictive control (MPC) to generate the optimal schedules for their flexible loads such HPs, EVs, and batteries;\n3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on the optimal schedules prior to the delivery time\n4. market clearing: match the demand and supply and clear the market;\n5. receiving results: receives the market clearing results for the delivery time after the market clearing;\n6. real-time control: use real-time controller to adjust the operating states of the flexible loads at the delivery time according to the electricity procured from the LEM;\n7. settlement: settle the consumption or generation soon after the electricity has been delivered\n\nThe steps 1 to 5 should be repeated for every rolling horizon prior to the delivery time step. Prosumers should check the clearing results from the previous rolling horizon to ensure that the procured electricity is sufficient for their energy demand at the time step of delivery."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply submission precedes local market clearing in the stated procedure. Scope: The ordered energy-exchange procedure repeated for each rolling horizon before delivery.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on to the optimal schedules prior to","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In general, prosumers must complete the following steps to achieve energy exchange in the LEM:\n1. forecasts: make forecasts about weather, demands, and electricity prices;\n2. model-predictive control: use the model-predictive control (MPC) to generate the optimal schedules for their flexible loads such HPs, EVs, and batteries;\n3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on the optimal schedules prior to the delivery time\n4. market clearing: match the demand and supply and clear the market;\n5. receiving results: receives the market clearing results for the delivery time after the market clearing;\n6. real-time control: use real-time controller to adjust the operating states of the flexible loads at the delivery time according to the electricity procured from the LEM;\n7. settlement: settle the consumption or generation soon after the electricity has been delivered\n\nThe steps 1 to 5 should be repeated for every rolling horizon prior to the delivery time step. Prosumers should check the clearing results from the previous rolling horizon to ensure that the procured electricity is sufficient for their energy demand at the time step of delivery."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market operator coordinates clearing by ensuring balance between total accepted consumption and generation. Scope: Accepted bids in the local two-sided auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e11"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The two-sided auction allows for consumption and production bids to be part of the same market clearing process. The market operator ensures a balance between total consumption and total generation among the accepted bids."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C006","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Buyers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a purchase allocation. Scope: Buyer-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The buyer's bid price is greater than or equal to the uniform local market price.","expression":"p_i^{bid} \\ge p^M \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\text{buyer } i \\text{ may receive a purchase allocation}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-p-market","v141-c-R003-theta-p-bid-i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C007","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Sellers meeting the stated clearing-price threshold are permitted to receive a sale allocation. Scope: Seller-side allocation permissions in the local uniform-price auction. Condition: The seller's offer price is less than or equal to the uniform local market price.","expression":"p_j^{offer} \\le p^M \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\text{seller } j \\text{ may receive a sale allocation}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-p-market","v141-c-R003-theta-p-offer-j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, the auction operates as a uniform price auction, with all accepted bids paying or receiving the same market price. All buyers who bid above or equal to this price can buy, while all sellers who sell below or equal to this price can sell."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C008","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The LEM clears every 15 min with a 24 h trading horizon. Scope: Rolling future-market clearing in the modeled LEM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Limited by the scope, the description of other parts of lemlab is omitted Th in this work. However, ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The LEM uses a future market design, which is the most common market design found in the literature [29]. Therefore, the LEM undergoes clearing every 15 min, with a 24 h trading horizon, allowing prosumers to trade electricity up to 24 h in advance. This allows the LEM to function as a day-ahead, intraday, or near real-time market. If prosumers are unable to fulfill their energy demand in one round of market clearing, they can continue submitting their bids in subsequent trading cycles. During settlement, any energy imbalances resulting from a deviation from the traded position lead to additional balancing costs."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C009","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local clearing must balance total accepted demand and total accepted supply. Scope: The balance constraint on accepted local auction quantities.","expression":"\\sum_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = \\sum_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-demand-bid-i","v141-c-R003-x-supply-offer-j"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-n-B","v141-c-R003-theta-n-S"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g01-e10"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C009","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"max SW = ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} u_i(d_i) − ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} c_j(s_j)\ns.t. ∑_{i=1}^{n_B} d_i = ∑_{j=1}^{n_S} s_j (1)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Visualization of a double-sided auction. The two-sided auction allows for consumption and pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The two-sided auction allows for consumption and production bids to be part of the same market clearing process. The market operator ensures a balance between total consumption and total generation among the accepted bids."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local market clearing occurs before the physical energy exchange at the delivery time step. Scope: Market clearing in the rolling pre-delivery workflow of the study LEM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on to the optimal schedules prior to","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In general, prosumers must complete the following steps to achieve energy exchange in the LEM:\n1. forecasts: make forecasts about weather, demands, and electricity prices;\n2. model-predictive control: use the model-predictive control (MPC) to generate the optimal schedules for their flexible loads such HPs, EVs, and batteries;\n3. submitting bids: send their bids and offers to the LEM based on the optimal schedules prior to the delivery time\n4. market clearing: match the demand and supply and clear the market;\n5. receiving results: receives the market clearing results for the delivery time after the market clearing;\n6. real-time control: use real-time controller to adjust the operating states of the flexible loads at the delivery time according to the electricity procured from the LEM;\n7. settlement: settle the consumption or generation soon after the electricity has been delivered\n\nThe steps 1 to 5 should be repeated for every rolling horizon prior to the delivery time step. Prosumers should check the clearing results from the previous rolling horizon to ensure that the procured electricity is sufficient for their energy demand at the time step of delivery."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. Timeline of the trading process in the LEM. to su Otherwise, they should continue bidding at","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Otherwise, they should continue bidding at later time steps until they have obtained enough electricity. During the delivery time step, the physical flow of energy takes place, and real-time control is activated to ensure precise consumption. Finally, the costs are settled based on the metering data that reflects the real consumption. The whole process is illustrated in Fig. 2."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market clearing process determines the local electricity price. Scope: Electricity pricing in the proposed local energy market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01"],"ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R011::v141-c-R011-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R011","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a so ute educt o o t e e e gy su p us s a ecause o t e lower solar radiation in winter. cl The compa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"LEMs aim to provide advantageous electricity prices by facilitating lower local market prices for all participants. Energy buyers can save costs by using electricity cheaper than the retailer prices, while energy sellers can earn more money compared to direct sales to the retailer. These electricity prices are determined by the market clearing process."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X001","symbol":"p_{t,bid}","meaning":"Demand-side (buying) bid price at time step t, as defined by the source's buying-side linear bid-price trajectory.","kind":"operational","domain":"Generated by Eq. (2) for t_d - ΔT ≤ t ≤ t_d, with p_max as the price ceiling and p_min as the price floor.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X002","symbol":"ΔT","meaning":"Trading horizon selected by the prosumer.","kind":"design_selection","domain":"6 h ≤ ΔT ≤ 24 h, as stated in the source.","unit":"h","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X002"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-demand-bid-i","symbol":"d_i","meaning":"Demand bid quantity for buyer i in the local two-sided auction, denoted d_i in the source's aggregate balance equation. The source does not explicitly distinguish submitted quantities from accepted quantities in the formula; the rule scope applies the balance to accepted local auction quantities as stated in C009 and supported by e11.","kind":"operational","domain":"Unspecified in source; symbol used as a demand-bid quantity in Eq. (1).","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e11"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-demand-bid-i"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-supply-offer-j","symbol":"s_j","meaning":"Supply offer quantity for seller j in the local two-sided auction, denoted s_j in the source's aggregate balance equation. The source does not explicitly distinguish submitted quantities from accepted quantities in the formula; the rule scope applies the balance to accepted local auction quantities as stated in C009 and supported by e11.","kind":"operational","domain":"Unspecified in source; symbol used as a supply-offer quantity in Eq. (1).","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e11"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-supply-offer-j"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-P001","symbol":"p_{max}","meaning":"Price ceiling.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-P001"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-P002","symbol":"p_{min}","meaning":"Price floor.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-P002"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-P003","symbol":"Δp","meaning":"Price increment in the next time step when bids are not accepted completely, defined by Eq. (4).","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\Delta p = (p_{max} - p_{min}) / \\Delta T"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-P003"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-n-B","symbol":"n_B","meaning":"Number of buyers in the local two-sided auction, as defined in the source.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-n-B"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-n-S","symbol":"n_S","meaning":"Number of sellers in the local two-sided auction, as defined in the source.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-n-S"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p-market","symbol":"p^M","meaning":"Uniform local market price in the local uniform-price auction, treated as the given threshold in the buyer and seller allocation-permission conditions.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p-market"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p-bid-i","symbol":"p_i^{bid}","meaning":"Buyer i's submitted bid price in the local uniform-price auction, as referenced by the buyer acceptance threshold.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p-bid-i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p-offer-j","symbol":"p_j^{offer}","meaning":"Seller j's offered or selling price in the local uniform-price auction, as referenced by the seller acceptance threshold.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p-offer-j"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","stage":"L5","subtype":"balanced_auction_allocation","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"Consumption and production bids are included in the same clearing round, and within the accepted bid range, Σ_{i=1}^{n_B}d_i=Σ_{j=1}^{n_S}s_j is maintained; a buy price p_i^{bid}≥p^M permits obtaining a purchase allocation, and a sell price p_j^{offer}≤p^M permits obtaining a sale allocation.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: purchase and sale quantities of the same auction round","Core relation: accepted demand and supply totals are balanced, and the corresponding price eligibility conditions are satisfied","Output: accepted purchase and sale allocations and unmet demand"],"variation_fields":["Clearing every 15 min, using a 24 h rolling trading look-ahead","Unmet demand may continue to be submitted in subsequent trading periods","In the original expression, d_i and s_j are called bid quantities; the accepted-quantity range is restricted by the accompanying text","The price threshold only provides allocation eligibility; it does not specify full-volume execution or same-price rationing rules"],"constraint_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C006","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C007","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C008","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C009"],"paper_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"clearing.local","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","retained_variants":["Consumption and production bids enter the same clearing round, and within the accepted bid range, Σ_{i=1}^{n_B}d_i=Σ_{j=1}^{n_S}s_j is maintained.","A buy price p_i^{bid}≥p^M permits a purchase allocation, and a sell price p_j^{offer}≤p^M permits a sale allocation; eligibility does not mean full-volume execution.","In the original expression, d_i and s_j are called bid quantities, and the accepted-quantity range is restricted by the accompanying text; no same-price rationing rules are given.","Clearing occurs every 15 min, using a 24 h rolling trading look-ahead; unmet demand may continue to be submitted in subsequent periods."],"evidence_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-fe986661377aea49","baseline_parent_code":"CLR060","secondary_class":"SC-L5-ce2697ec42590f31","category":{"id":"SC-L5-ce2697ec42590f31","stage":"L5","label_zh":"Balanced trade allocation subject to price-based trading permission","definition_zh":"In the same auction round, determine the accepted purchase and sale quantities so that accepted demand and supply totals are balanced and the allocation-eligibility conditions of buy and sell bids relative to the clearing price are satisfied; eligibility is not presumed to imply full-volume execution.","main_identity_axes":["Decision object: purchase and sale quantities accepted by the auction","Allocation conditions: balance of supply and demand quantities and two-sided price eligibility","Statement type: quantity allocation and its feasible bounds"],"inclusion_criteria":["Directly expresses the balance relation between accepted purchase and sale quantities in the same round.","At the same time, it specifies allocation eligibility based on buy and sell bids relative to the clearing price.","Unexpanded execution ratios or same-price allocation rules are not supplied."],"exclusion_criteria":["Only declares a welfare objective without expressing the above quantity allocation relation.","Only calculates a marginal index or selects the set of agents permitted to trade.","Only specifies same-side price priority ordering or pairwise matching of the smaller quantity.","Only describes conservation of exchanges within a community."],"supporting_unit_ids":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"Allocate purchase and sale quantities in the same auction round so that the total accepted supply and demand balance and the allocation eligibility conditions for buy and sell bids relative to the clearing price are satisfied.","identity_fields":["Object: accepted purchase and sale quantities in the same auction round","Allocation conditions: accepted-quantity balance and two-sided price eligibility","Statement type: quantity allocation and feasible bounds"],"member_unit_ids":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-a-M01::clearing.local"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/299"});
